  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "The frequency $v$ of the radiation emitted by an atom when an electron jumps from one orbit to another is given by $=\\mathrm{k} \\delta \\mathrm{E}$, where $\\mathrm{k}$ is a constant and $\\delta \\mathrm{E}$ is the change in energy level due to the transition. Then dimension of $\\mathrm{k}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "hTqwc",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{ML}^{2} \\mathrm{~T}^{-2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "zN8jX",
      "text": "the same dimension of angular momentum",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "uLUGd",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{ML}^{2} \\mathrm{~T}^{-1}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "7xoVw",
      "text": "$\\mathrm{M}^{-1} \\mathrm{~L}^{-2} \\mathrm{~T}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint: \r\n$v=k \\delta E$\r\n$[k]=\\left[\\frac{v}{\\delta E}\\right]=\\frac{\\left[T^{-1}\\right]}{\\left[M L^{2} T^{-2}\\right]}$\r\n$[k]=\\left[M^{-} L^{-2} T^{1}\\right]$",
